{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01HRyuShRn5AtSzEW6yBkRKf","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user wants me to generate detailed predicted experimental results for all \"planned\" experiments in the experiment_plan, based on the \"median\" tier definition. I need to provide realistic predictions with rationales for each experiment.\n\nLet me carefully go through each planned experiment and generate predictions consistent with the median tier definition.\n\nKey median tier parameters:\n- EDD ≈ 3\n- DCOL has advantage but not overwhelming (+3-7pp over best baseline)\n- Cross-model transfer meets gate (≥45%) but with fluctuation\n- Atlas shows depth 4-5 feature overlap, some non-monotonic phenomena\n\n\n- Downstream curation shows positive but marginal statistical significance, with pooled 6-class accuracy ranging from 52-62%, cross-model leave-one-out transfer between 42-52%, and adjacent AUC within the EDD range hitting 72-80%.\n- Feature monotonicity scores for the top 5 features sit around 70-85%, while the median EDD across combinations stays at 3, and delta improvements over baseline hover between 3-7 percentage points.\n- The MVP results are solid: 4-class accuracy of 0.782 using Random Forest on Pythia with nucleus sampling, strong pairwise AUCs, and the top predictive features being variance in surprisal, percentile PPL metrics, and mean surprisal.\n- Now I'm looking at plan_002 with OLMo-1B, which uses a different architecture and Dolma's text-focused training data, so I'd expect similar but slightly shifted patterns compared to Pythia.\n- Plan_003 with GPT-2 XL should reveal stronger degradation signals at shallow depths since it's the most studied in collapse literature and uses WebText training data.\n- Plan_004 focuses on DCOL training with DeBERTa and contrastive learning, targeting 6-class accuracy between 0.52-0.62.\n- Plan_005 tests cross-model generalization with leave-one-model-out, expecting accuracy around 0.42-0.52 with some rotations passing the 45% gate threshold.\n- Plan_007 is examining strategy-specific effects through leave-one-strategy-out validation.\n\nStrategy generalization should be easier than model generalization since strategies affect surface statistics more uniformly. Plan_008 tests whether end-to-end DeBERTa training matches feature-based approaches, suggesting both capture similar information. Plan_009 expects DCOL to outperform baselines by 3-7 percentage points. Plan_010 ablates components to confirm each contributes meaningfully without any single component dominating. Plan_011 extends depth to 5 generations to confirm saturation around depth 3-4, validating the EDD≈3 estimate. Plan_012 tests granularity levels, with 4-class as the optimal setting and 6-class showing degradation but staying above chance. Plan_013 evaluates downstream curation, expecting 2-5% perplexity reduction compared to binary classification with marginal significance.\n\nNow I'm setting up the cross-scale transfer experiments—plan_014 will probe whether a 7B model trained on small-scale data transfers to larger models with some performance drop, and plan_015 will check how well wild-data calibration correlates with quality proxies. I should structure all these expectations in a detailed YAML format with specific metric targets.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":10200,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":10200},"output_tokens":27,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"59c1aef7-b7d0-4e34-b364-7145a430c46b","uuid":"fc8225f8-33c3-4922-9130-66118721f3e3"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01HRyuShRn5AtSzEW6yBkRKf","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"```yaml\ntier: median\nnarrative_guidance: >\n  EDD≈3是核心科学发现，论文叙事围绕\"ordinal depth estimation在EDD边界内可行\"展开。\n  DCOL优于baseline但优势中等（+3-7pp），叙事重心从方法突破转向\"序数框架+Atlas\"的组合贡献。\n  Atlas权重上升为论文核心——文档化递归退化的边界和模式对model collapse社区直接有用。\n  Claim 3缩减为proof-of-concept。跨模型泛化诚实报告per-rotation结果，弱rotation作为limitation。\n  有效粒度声明降级：6-class数字报告但承认depth 4+坍缩，实际可行粒度为4-class（depths 0-3）。\n\nimagined_experiments:\n  - name: \"OLMo-1B recursive chain benchmark\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_002\"\n    description: \"OLMo-1B在3种策略下生成5层递归链，提取19维统计特征，RF分类\"\n    expected_results:\n      full_4class_acc: 0.754\n      full_4class_acc_ci: [0.740, 0.768]\n      full_mae: 0.268\n      full_auc_0v1: 0.994\n      full_auc_1v2: 0.838\n      full_auc_2v3: 0.771\n      filtered_4class_acc: 0.789\n      filtered_4class_acc_ci: [0.775, 0.803]\n      filtered_mae: 0.225\n      best_model: \"RandomForest\"\n      top_features: [\"var_surprisal\", \"mean_ppl\", \"p90_ppl\", \"zipf_alpha\", \"mean_surprisal\"]\n      feature_dim: 19\n      samples_per_depth_per_strategy: ~1200\n    result_rationale: >\n      OLMo-1B在Dolma上训练，分布与Pythia的Pile有差异。Dolma以清洗后的web text为主，\n      初始生成（depth 0→1）的分布偏移略小于Pythia，导致depth 0v1的AUC微降（0.994 vs 0.998）。\n      但OLMo的Dolma训练使其对web-text domain更稳定，depth 2v3退化信号略弱（0.771 vs 0.801），\n      因为OLMo的生成在浅层更\"像人类\"，深层退化启动更晚。整体4-class acc低于Pythia约3pp，\n      符合median档\"信号真实但模型间有波动\"的预期。var_surprisal仍是最强特征，\n      但zipf_alpha在OLMo上排名上升——OLMo的tokenizer和训练数据使词频分布对递归深度更敏感。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: OLMo-1B per-strategy 4-class accuracy\"\n        rows:\n          - strategy: \"nucleus_p0.95\"\n            acc_4class: 0.768\n            mae: 0.252\n            auc_0v1: 0.995\n            auc_1v2: 0.849\n            auc_2v3: 0.784\n          - strategy: \"temperature_0.9\"\n            acc_4class: 0.741\n            mae: 0.281\n            auc_0v1: 0.993\n            auc_1v2: 0.827\n            auc_2v3: 0.758\n          - strategy: \"topk_50\"\n            acc_4class: 0.752\n            mae: 0.271\n            auc_0v1: 0.994\n            auc_1v2: 0.839\n            auc_2v3: 0.770\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: OLMo per-strategy adjacent-depth AUC曲线，显示3种策略在depth 2→3处均出现明显下降\"\n    analysis: >\n      OLMo结果确认递归退化信号跨模型存在但强度有差异。temperature策略在OLMo上表现最弱，\n      因为τ=0.9引入的随机性与OLMo自身生成的多样性叠加，模糊了深度信号。\n      这预示cross-model泛化中OLMo作为held-out时可能是较难的rotation。\n\n  - name: \"GPT-2 XL recursive chain benchmark\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_003\"\n    description: \"GPT-2 XL 1.5B在3种策略下生成5层递归链，提取19维统计特征，RF分类\"\n    expected_results:\n      full_4class_acc: 0.798\n      full_4class_acc_ci: [0.785, 0.811]\n      full_mae: 0.218\n      full_auc_0v1: 0.998\n      full_auc_1v2: 0.874\n      full_auc_2v3: 0.812\n      filtered_4class_acc: 0.831\n      filtered_4class_acc_ci: [0.818, 0.844]\n      filtered_mae: 0.183\n      best_model: \"RandomForest\"\n      top_features: [\"var_surprisal\", \"p90_ppl\", \"mean_ppl\", \"mean_surprisal\", \"p75_ppl\"]\n      feature_dim: 19\n      samples_per_depth_per_strategy: ~1200\n    result_rationale: >\n      GPT-2 XL是collapse文献中最被研究的模型，其WebText训练集相对较小且老旧。\n      关键：GPT-2 XL的生成能力弱于Pythia和OLMo，递归生成退化更快更明显，\n      导致相邻深度间的统计差异更大。depth 0v1的AUC（0.998）与Pythia持平，\n      但depth 1v2（0.874 vs 0.861）和depth 2v3（0.812 vs 0.801）均高于Pythia。\n      这意味着GPT-2 XL的EDD可能略高于3（但在6-class下仍然depth 4+坍缩）。\n      4-class acc 0.798略高于Pythia的0.782，因为GPT-2 XL的退化信号更强。\n      top features排名与Pythia几乎一致，说明var_surprisal作为核心信号具有跨模型稳定性。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: GPT-2 XL per-strategy 4-class accuracy\"\n        rows:\n          - strategy: \"nucleus_p0.95\"\n            acc_4class: 0.812\n            mae: 0.204\n            auc_0v1: 0.998\n            auc_1v2: 0.885\n            auc_2v3: 0.823\n          - strategy: \"temperature_0.9\"\n            acc_4class: 0.783\n            mae: 0.234\n            auc_0v1: 0.997\n            auc_1v2: 0.861\n            auc_2v3: 0.798\n          - strategy: \"topk_50\"\n            acc_4class: 0.799\n            mae: 0.217\n            auc_0v1: 0.998\n            auc_1v2: 0.876\n            auc_2v3: 0.815\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: GPT-2 XL与Pythia的adjacent-depth AUC对比，GPT-2 XL在所有对上均略高\"\n    analysis: >\n      GPT-2 XL展现最强的深度信号，符合其作为\"能力较弱模型退化更快\"的预期。\n      这对Atlas叙事有利——不同模型的退化速率不同，但模式（monotonic decrease in AUC）一致。\n      GPT-2 XL的强信号也意味着在cross-model实验中，它作为训练集的一部分会贡献最多信息，\n      作为held-out测试集则最容易通过gate。\n\n  - name: \"DCOL contrastive ordinal training\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_004\"\n    description: \"DeBERTa-v3-large编码器 + 多margin N-pair contrastive loss，6-class depth estimation\"\n    expected_results:\n      dcol_6class_acc_pooled: 0.571\n      dcol_6class_acc_ci: [0.556, 0.586]\n      dcol_mae_6class: 0.462\n      dcol_4class_acc: 0.823\n      dcol_4class_acc_ci: [0.811, 0.835]\n      dcol_mae_4class: 0.192\n      dcol_auc_0v1: 0.999\n      dcol_auc_1v2: 0.912\n      dcol_auc_2v3: 0.856\n      dcol_auc_3v4: 0.714\n      dcol_auc_4v5: 0.628\n      best_lr: 2.0e-5\n      best_margin_schedule: \"learned_non_uniform\"\n      convergence_epoch: 7\n      training_hours_actual: 12.5\n    result_rationale: >\n      DCOL利用DeBERTa编码器从原始文本学习表示，contrastive ordinal loss强制相邻深度的embedding\n      距离反映实际退化幅度。6-class pooled acc 0.571处于median范围[0.52,0.62]中段。\n      关键：DCOL相比RF+features的提升集中在depth 1-3的区分（AUC 1v2从0.86→0.91，2v3从0.80→0.86），\n      因为contrastive learning能捕捉features无法编码的微妙语义退化模式。\n      但depth 3v4的AUC仅0.714——刚好在EDD边界上，depth 4v5的0.628接近随机（chance~0.5）。\n      这证实EDD≈3：DCOL在depth 0-3上显著优于RF，但无法突破depth 3+的信号天花板。\n      4-class acc 0.823高于RF的0.782（pooled across 3 models），验证了contrastive learning\n      在EDD内的有效性。non_uniform learned margins优于fixed margins，\n      因为实际inter-depth距离高度不均匀（depth 0→1远大于depth 2→3）。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: DCOL vs RF feature-based, pooled across 3 models × 3 strategies\"\n        rows:\n          - method: \"DCOL (DeBERTa + contrastive)\"\n            acc_6class: 0.571\n            mae_6class: 0.462\n            acc_4class: 0.823\n            mae_4class: 0.192\n          - method: \"RF + 19 features\"\n            acc_6class: 0.497\n            mae_6class: 0.538\n            acc_4class: 0.778\n            mae_4class: 0.241\n          - method: \"CORAL (DeBERTa + fixed margin)\"\n            acc_6class: 0.538\n            mae_6class: 0.491\n            acc_4class: 0.806\n            mae_4class: 0.211\n          - method: \"CE (DeBERTa + cross-entropy)\"\n            acc_6class: 0.519\n            mae_6class: 0.512\n            acc_4class: 0.793\n            mae_4class: 0.224\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: DCOL训练loss曲线 + per-class accuracy随epoch变化，depth 4-5的accuracy在epoch 4后plateau\"\n      - \"Fig: Learned margin值可视化——margin(0,1) >> margin(2,3) >> margin(3,4)，反映退化的非均匀性\"\n    analysis: >\n      DCOL在EDD边界内（depth 0-3）的优势明确，但对depth 4+无能为力。\n      这支持median叙事：方法有效但有天花板，天花板由信号本身（而非方法）决定。\n      CORAL作为ablation的中间点（0.538 vs DCOL 0.571 vs CE 0.519）说明\n      ordinal inductive bias有帮助，learned margins在此基础上进一步提升。\n      但DCOL vs CORAL仅+3.3pp，说明增益部分来自ordinal structure本身而非contrastive learning独有。\n\n  - name: \"Leave-one-model-out generalization\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_005\"\n    description: \"3个rotation：每次留一个模型族作test，用另外两个训练DCOL\"\n    expected_results:\n      rotation_hold_pythia:\n        train_on: [\"OLMo-1B\", \"GPT-2 XL\"]\n        test_on: \"Pythia-1.4B\"\n        acc_6class: 0.483\n        acc_4class: 0.721\n        mae_6class: 0.547\n      rotation_hold_olmo:\n        train_on: [\"Pythia-1.4B\", \"GPT-2 XL\"]\n        test_on: \"OLMo-1B\"\n        acc_6class: 0.421\n        acc_4class: 0.673\n        mae_6class: 0.601\n      rotation_hold_gpt2xl:\n        train_on: [\"Pythia-1.4B\", \"OLMo-1B\"]\n        test_on: \"GPT-2 XL\"\n        acc_6class: 0.507\n        acc_4class: 0.748\n        mae_6class: 0.521\n      cross_model_loo_6class_acc_mean: 0.470\n      cross_model_loo_6class_acc_std: 0.036\n      cross_model_loo_4class_acc_mean: 0.714\n      gate_pass_count: \"2/3 rotations ≥ 0.45 (6-class), OLMo rotation at 0.421 misses\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      跨模型泛化是median档的核心挑战。mean 6-class acc 0.470处于[0.42,0.52]范围内。\n      Hold-OLMo是最弱rotation（0.421，未通过0.45 gate）：OLMo在Dolma上训练，\n      其生成分布与Pile-trained Pythia和WebText-trained GPT-2 XL差异最大。\n      Pythia和GPT-2 XL都在\"early web text\"类型数据上训练，彼此更相似，\n      所以hold-GPT2XL rotation最强（0.507）——Pythia+OLMo的组合已覆盖足够多样性。\n      Hold-Pythia居中（0.483），因为OLMo+GPT2XL的组合提供了合理的训练分布。\n      4-class acc均显著高于6-class，再次确认depth 4+的信号不跨模型迁移。\n      std=0.036反映\"有波动\"的median特征——不是所有rotation都稳定通过。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: Leave-one-model-out 6-class results\"\n        rows:\n          - rotation: \"Hold Pythia\"\n            acc_6class: 0.483\n            acc_4class: 0.721\n            mae: 0.547\n            gate_45: \"PASS\"\n          - rotation: \"Hold OLMo\"\n            acc_6class: 0.421\n            acc_4class: 0.673\n            mae: 0.601\n            gate_45: \"FAIL\"\n          - rotation: \"Hold GPT-2 XL\"\n            acc_6class: 0.507\n            acc_4class: 0.748\n            mae: 0.521\n            gate_45: \"PASS\"\n          - rotation: \"Mean ± std\"\n            acc_6class: \"0.470 ± 0.036\"\n            acc_4class: \"0.714 ± 0.031\"\n            mae: \"0.556 ± 0.033\"\n            gate_45: \"2/3\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: 3-rotation confusion matrices并排，Hold-OLMo显示depth 2和depth 3高度混淆\"\n      - \"Fig: Per-rotation per-depth accuracy heatmap，depth 0在所有rotation上 > 90%\"\n    analysis: >\n      OLMo rotation的失败需要在论文中诚实报告为limitation。叙事可以是：\n      \"跨模型泛化在架构/数据相似的模型间成立，但对训练分布差异大的模型需要域适应\"。\n      4-class acc 0.714 mean说明\"在EDD内的粗粒度估计\"仍然跨模型可行，\n      这支持降级后的Claim 1声明。补充feature importance drift分析解释OLMo为什么难。\n\n  - name: \"Depth Degradation Atlas\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_006\"\n    description: \"9个model×strategy combo的特征单调性分析、EDD计算、跨模型/策略热力图\"\n    expected_results:\n      edd_per_combo:\n        pythia_nucleus: 3\n        pythia_temperature: 3\n        pythia_topk: 3\n        olmo_nucleus: 3\n        olmo_temperature: 2\n        olmo_topk: 3\n        gpt2xl_nucleus: 4\n        gpt2xl_temperature: 3\n        gpt2xl_topk: 3\n      edd_median: 3\n      edd_mean: 3.0\n      edd_min: 2\n      edd_max: 4\n      monotonicity_score_top5_mean: 0.782\n      monotonicity_score_top5_range: [0.71, 0.85]\n      top5_features_by_monotonicity: [\"var_surprisal\", \"p90_ppl\", \"mean_ppl\", \"zipf_alpha\", \"mean_surprisal\"]\n      feature_monotonicity_var_surprisal: 0.847\n      feature_monotonicity_p90_ppl: 0.823\n      feature_monotonicity_mean_ppl: 0.801\n      feature_monotonicity_zipf_alpha: 0.768\n      feature_monotonicity_mean_surprisal: 0.752\n      non_monotonic_combos: [\"olmo_temperature_depth3→4_mean_ppl\", \"pythia_topk_depth4→5_var_surprisal\"]\n      min_adjacent_auc_within_edd: 0.771\n    result_rationale: >\n      EDD median=3横跨9个combo，但分布有意义的变化。GPT-2 XL nucleus是唯一EDD=4的combo，\n      因为GPT-2 XL退化最快（前述），nucleus采样保留了最多信号。OLMo temperature是唯一EDD=2的combo，\n      因为OLMo的生成多样性本就高，叠加temperature的随机性导致depth 2→3的信号就已饱和。\n      这种跨combo的EDD变化本身就是Atlas的核心科学贡献——EDD不是一个固定常数而是取决于模型能力和解码策略。\n      top5特征的单调性得分mean 0.782处于[0.7,0.85]范围。var_surprisal最高（0.847），\n      因为递归生成使surprisal分布progressively narrowing——这是最稳定的退化信号。\n      两个非单调combo出现在depth 3→4之后，符合\"EDD边界后信号坍缩\"的预期。\n      min_adjacent_auc_within_edd=0.771（出现在OLMo temperature的depth 1v2），处于[0.72,0.80]范围。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: EDD per model × strategy\"\n        rows:\n          - model: \"Pythia-1.4B\"\n            nucleus: 3\n            temperature: 3\n            topk: 3\n          - model: \"OLMo-1B\"\n            nucleus: 3\n            temperature: 2\n            topk: 3\n          - model: \"GPT-2 XL\"\n            nucleus: 4\n            temperature: 3\n            topk: 3\n      - name: \"Table: Top-10 feature monotonicity scores (mean across 9 combos)\"\n        rows:\n          - feature: \"var_surprisal\"\n            mono_score: 0.847\n            rank_stability: \"1/9 combos rank 1\"\n          - feature: \"p90_ppl\"\n            mono_score: 0.823\n            rank_stability: \"6/9 combos rank ≤ 3\"\n          - feature: \"mean_ppl\"\n            mono_score: 0.801\n            rank_stability: \"7/9 combos rank ≤ 4\"\n          - feature: \"zipf_alpha\"\n            mono_score: 0.768\n            rank_stability: \"5/9 combos rank ≤ 5\"\n          - feature: \"mean_surprisal\"\n            mono_score: 0.752\n            rank_stability: \"8/9 combos rank ≤ 6\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: 9-panel heatmap（3 models × 3 strategies），每panel显示19个特征在6个depth上的z-score，EDD边界用虚线标注\"\n      - \"Fig: var_surprisal在9个combo上的depth-wise分布boxplot，显示depth 0-3单调递减，depth 4-5重叠\"\n      - \"Fig: EDD boundary可视化——adjacent-depth AUC随depth递减，0.72阈值线标注EDD截断点\"\n      - \"Fig: 非单调异常案例的feature trajectory（OLMo temperature的mean_ppl在depth 3→4回升）\"\n    analysis: >\n      Atlas是median档下论文的核心贡献。EDD=3的中位数意味着\"ordinal depth estimation在4级粒度上可行\"，\n      这本身就是对model collapse社区的直接贡献——之前没有人系统量化\"从哪个depth开始区分变得不可能\"。\n      EDD跨combo的变化（2-4）提供了丰富的分析空间：为什么OLMo+temperature最早饱和？\n      为什么GPT-2 XL+nucleus能多撑一层？这些问题直接关联模型能力和解码策略的交互效应。\n      非单调现象（2/9 combos在EDD之后）可以解释为\"信号坍缩后的噪声震荡\"而非真实的非单调退化。\n\n  - name: \"Leave-one-strategy-out robustness\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_007\"\n    description: \"3个rotation：每次留一种策略作test，用另外两种训练DCOL\"\n    expected_results:\n      rotation_hold_nucleus:\n        train_on: [\"temperature\", \"topk\"]\n        test_on: \"nucleus\"\n        acc_6class: 0.528\n        acc_4class: 0.786\n      rotation_hold_temperature:\n        train_on: [\"nucleus\", \"topk\"]\n        test_on: \"temperature\"\n        acc_6class: 0.492\n        acc_4class: 0.753\n      rotation_hold_topk:\n        train_on: [\"nucleus\", \"temperature\"]\n        test_on: \"topk\"\n        acc_6class: 0.541\n        acc_4class: 0.798\n      strategy_loo_6class_acc_mean: 0.520\n      strategy_loo_6class_acc_std: 0.021\n    result_rationale: >\n      策略间泛化优于模型间泛化（mean 0.520 vs 0.470），因为不同解码策略影响的是生成文本的\n      表面统计特性（多样性、重复率），而递归退化的核心信号（surprisal variance压缩、\n      perplexity drift）跨策略更稳定。Hold-temperature最弱（0.492）是因为temperature采样\n      产生的分布与nucleus/topk的截断采样在尾部行为上差异最大——temperature不截断分布，\n      而是rescale整个logit空间，导致生成文本的统计profile不同。\n      Hold-topk最强（0.541）是因为topk_50与nucleus_0.95在实际效果上最接近\n      （都是尾部截断，只是截断方式不同），所以nucleus训练集已包含了大部分topk的信号。\n      std=0.021远小于cross-model的0.036，说明策略间差异比模型间差异小。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: Leave-one-strategy-out results\"\n        rows:\n          - rotation: \"Hold nucleus\"\n            acc_6class: 0.528\n            acc_4class: 0.786\n          - rotation: \"Hold temperature\"\n            acc_6class: 0.492\n            acc_4class: 0.753\n          - rotation: \"Hold topk\"\n            acc_6class: 0.541\n            acc_4class: 0.798\n          - rotation: \"Mean ± std\"\n            acc_6class: \"0.520 ± 0.021\"\n            acc_4class: \"0.779 ± 0.019\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: Strategy-out vs Model-out泛化gap对比bar chart\"\n    analysis: >\n      策略泛化比模型泛化容易的结论对论文positioning有利——说明depth信号主要与模型能力相关，\n      而非解码策略的artifact。这强化了Atlas中\"模型能力决定EDD\"的叙事。\n      Hold-temperature的相对弱势可引出discussion：temperature采样作为最\"自由\"的策略，\n      其生成文本的统计分布最不受约束，可能需要专门的domain adaptation。\n\n  - name: \"DeBERTa end-to-end classifier\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_008\"\n    description: \"DeBERTa-v3-large直接text→6-class depth分类，无手工特征\"\n    expected_results:\n      e2e_6class_acc: 0.553\n      e2e_6class_acc_ci: [0.537, 0.569]\n      e2e_mae_6class: 0.478\n      e2e_4class_acc: 0.809\n      e2e_4class_acc_ci: [0.796, 0.822]\n      e2e_mae_4class: 0.206\n      e2e_auc_0v1: 0.998\n      e2e_auc_1v2: 0.897\n      e2e_auc_2v3: 0.838\n      e2e_auc_3v4: 0.698\n      e2e_auc_4v5: 0.614\n      training_hours: 9.2\n      best_lr: 1.0e-5\n    result_rationale: >\n      End-to-end DeBERTa（CE loss）的6-class acc 0.553略低于DCOL的0.571，\n      但高于RF+features的0.497。这是median档的典型结果：end-to-end能学到features\n      无法捕捉的语义退化信号（如coherence loss、topic drift），但没有DCOL的ordinal\n      inductive bias，它在相邻深度的区分上不如DCOL精确——特别是depth 2v3（0.838 vs 0.856）\n      和depth 3v4（0.698 vs 0.714）的AUC差距。End-to-end不如DCOL的原因是CE loss\n      将每个class独立对待，不利用ordinal structure，而递归深度本质上是有序的。\n      但end-to-end优于RF说明原始文本中确实存在features未编码的退化信号。\n      这对论文叙事的含义：DCOL = end-to-end表示能力 + ordinal structure，两者都有贡献。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: End-to-end vs DCOL vs RF\"\n        rows:\n          - method: \"DCOL (contrastive ordinal)\"\n            acc_6class: 0.571\n            mae_6class: 0.462\n            acc_4class: 0.823\n          - method: \"DeBERTa E2E (CE)\"\n            acc_6class: 0.553\n            mae_6class: 0.478\n            acc_4class: 0.809\n          - method: \"RF + 19 features\"\n            acc_6class: 0.497\n            mae_6class: 0.538\n            acc_4class: 0.778\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: 三种方法的per-depth accuracy雷达图，DCOL在depth 2-3上优势最明显\"\n    analysis: >\n      DCOL vs E2E仅+1.8pp（6-class），这在median档下说明contrastive ordinal loss的增益\n      存在但不压倒性。论文需要将此差距诚实报告并通过ablation（plan_010）分解贡献来源。\n\n  - name: \"Baseline battery\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_009\"\n    description: \"7个baseline：DivEye features回归、perplexity回归、CORAL、CE、zero-shot LLM、binary ensemble、LOKI features\"\n    expected_results:\n      baselines:\n        diveye_ordinal_regression:\n          acc_6class: 0.432\n          mae_6class: 0.612\n          acc_4class: 0.698\n        perplexity_regression:\n          acc_6class: 0.389\n          mae_6class: 0.673\n          acc_4class: 0.651\n        coral_deberta:\n          acc_6class: 0.538\n          mae_6class: 0.491\n          acc_4class: 0.806\n        ce_deberta:\n          acc_6class: 0.519\n          mae_6class: 0.512\n          acc_4class: 0.793\n        zeroshot_llm_gpt4o:\n          acc_6class: 0.287\n          mae_6class: 0.892\n          acc_4class: 0.418\n        binary_ensemble_cascade:\n          acc_6class: 0.461\n          mae_6class: 0.574\n          acc_4class: 0.723\n        loki_features_regression:\n          acc_6class: 0.408\n          mae_6class: 0.641\n          acc_4class: 0.672\n      best_baseline: \"coral_deberta\"\n      best_baseline_6class_acc: 0.538\n      dcol_delta_over_best_baseline_pp: 3.3\n      dcol_delta_over_best_nonordinal_pp: 5.2\n    result_rationale: >\n      CORAL是最强baseline（0.538），因为它也利用了ordinal structure，与DCOL共享DeBERTa backbone。\n      DCOL vs CORAL的+3.3pp处于median的[3,7]范围下端，说明DCOL的增量贡献（learnable margins +\n      contrastive loss + strategy conditioning）存在但中等。CE DeBERTa次之（0.519），\n      说明DeBERTa的表示能力本身就很强，ordinal bias带来的额外增益约2pp。\n      DivEye features（0.432）比RF+19 features（0.497）低，因为DivEye的特征是为binary detection\n      设计的，缺少var_surprisal等对depth敏感的特征。Zero-shot LLM表现最差（0.287，接近\n      6-class chance 16.7%但显著高于），说明LLM的深度判断能力很弱——深度不是surface-level可感知的属性。\n      Binary ensemble cascade（先判binary再细分）达到0.461，优于feature regression但弱于\n      end-to-end方法，因为cascade的error propagation导致浅层误差累积。\n      DCOL delta +3.3pp在median范围内偏低，叙事需要强调\"框架+Atlas\"而非\"方法突破\"。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: Full baseline comparison (pooled across 3 models × 3 strategies)\"\n        rows:\n          - method: \"DCOL (ours)\"\n            acc_6class: 0.571\n            mae_6class: 0.462\n            acc_4class: 0.823\n            delta_vs_best: \"+3.3pp\"\n          - method: \"CORAL (DeBERTa)\"\n            acc_6class: 0.538\n            mae_6class: 0.491\n            acc_4class: 0.806\n            delta_vs_best: \"—\"\n          - method: \"CE (DeBERTa)\"\n            acc_6class: 0.519\n            mae_6class: 0.512\n            acc_4class: 0.793\n            delta_vs_best: \"-1.9pp\"\n          - method: \"RF + 19 features\"\n            acc_6class: 0.497\n            mae_6class: 0.538\n            acc_4class: 0.778\n            delta_vs_best: \"-4.1pp\"\n          - method: \"Binary cascade\"\n            acc_6class: 0.461\n            mae_6class: 0.574\n            acc_4class: 0.723\n            delta_vs_best: \"-7.7pp\"\n          - method: \"DivEye features\"\n            acc_6class: 0.432\n            mae_6class: 0.612\n            acc_4class: 0.698\n            delta_vs_best: \"-10.6pp\"\n          - method: \"LOKI features\"\n            acc_6class: 0.408\n            mae_6class: 0.641\n            acc_4class: 0.672\n            delta_vs_best: \"-13.0pp\"\n          - method: \"Perplexity regression\"\n            acc_6class: 0.389\n            mae_6class: 0.673\n            acc_4class: 0.651\n            delta_vs_best: \"-14.9pp\"\n          - method: \"Zero-shot GPT-4o\"\n            acc_6class: 0.287\n            mae_6class: 0.892\n            acc_4class: 0.418\n            delta_vs_best: \"-25.1pp\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: 所有方法的6-class acc bar chart，按性能排序，chance line标注\"\n      - \"Fig: MAE vs accuracy scatter plot，DCOL在Pareto前沿\"\n    analysis: >\n      Baseline battery确认DCOL优于所有baseline但优势中等。CORAL作为最强competitor\n      说明ordinal structure是关键——DCOL的额外+3.3pp来自learned margins和contrastive learning，\n      但大部分gain来自ordinal formulation本身。这强化median叙事的重心：\n      \"ordinal框架是核心贡献，DCOL是该框架下的一个strong实现\"。\n      Zero-shot LLM的失败是一个有趣的negative result，值得在paper中简短讨论。\n\n  - name: \"DCOL component ablation\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_010\"\n    description: \"移除surprisal anchors / learnable margins / strategy conditioning各一个，测量增量贡献\"\n    expected_results:\n      full_dcol: {acc_6class: 0.571, mae_6class: 0.462}\n      ablation_no_surprisal_anchors: {acc_6class: 0.558, mae_6class: 0.475, delta_pp: -1.3}\n      ablation_no_learnable_margins: {acc_6class: 0.547, mae_6class: 0.485, delta_pp: -2.4}\n      ablation_no_strategy_conditioning: {acc_6class: 0.562, mae_6class: 0.469, delta_pp: -0.9}\n      ablation_none_of_three: {acc_6class: 0.531, mae_6class: 0.498, delta_pp: -4.0}\n    result_rationale: >\n      Learnable margins的消融影响最大（-2.4pp），因为inter-depth距离的非均匀性是\n      递归退化的核心特征——fixed margins迫使模型假设所有相邻depth等距，这与实际不符。\n      Surprisal anchors的消融影响次之（-1.3pp），因为var_surprisal是最强特征，\n      将其嵌入anchor selection有助于contrastive learning聚焦于最有信息量的样本对。\n      Strategy conditioning影响最小（-0.9pp），因为在pooled setting下策略间差异\n      已经被训练数据的多样性部分覆盖——conditioning的主要作用是在per-strategy evaluation\n      上提升，pooled数字上反映较弱。三个组件全部移除等价于vanilla DeBERTa + N-pair loss，\n      acc降至0.531，仍高于CORAL（0.538→此处应低于CORAL），说明N-pair contrastive loss\n      本身相比CORAL的rank loss有约-0.7pp的差距，三个text-specific modifications\n      弥补了这个差距并额外提升+4.0pp。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: DCOL ablation\"\n        rows:\n          - variant: \"Full DCOL\"\n            acc_6class: 0.571\n            delta: \"—\"\n          - variant: \"– strategy conditioning\"\n            acc_6class: 0.562\n            delta: \"-0.9\"\n          - variant: \"– surprisal anchors\"\n            acc_6class: 0.558\n            delta: \"-1.3\"\n          - variant: \"– learnable margins\"\n            acc_6class: 0.547\n            delta: \"-2.4\"\n          - variant: \"– all three (vanilla contrastive)\"\n            acc_6class: 0.531\n            delta: \"-4.0\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: Ablation waterfall chart，从vanilla到full DCOL的累积增益\"\n    analysis: >\n      每个组件贡献1-2.4pp，没有单一组件是决定性的。这对median叙事的含义：\n      DCOL的三个text-specific modifications各自有小但一致的贡献，\n      组合起来提供了4pp的总增益。论文应将此framing为\"method engineering\"而非\"method breakthrough\"。\n\n  - name: \"Depth extension to 5+ generations and EDD analysis\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_011\"\n    description: \"Pythia链延伸到depth 5，分析depth 3-5的信号饱和\"\n    expected_results:\n      pythia_extended_auc_3v4: 0.708\n      pythia_extended_auc_4v5: 0.621\n      pythia_extended_auc_5v6: 0.573\n      feature_overlap_depth4_5_bhattacharyya: 0.82\n      feature_overlap_depth5_6_bhattacharyya: 0.91\n      edd_pythia_extended: 3\n      depth4_5_top_feature_rank_change: \"zipf_alpha从rank 4升至rank 2，var_surprisal从rank 1降至rank 3\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      延伸到depth 5-6后，AUC持续下降：3v4=0.708（已低于原EDD阈值0.72），4v5=0.621，\n      5v6=0.573（接近random的0.5）。Bhattacharyya overlap从depth 4-5的0.82升至depth 5-6的0.91，\n      说明特征分布高度重叠。EDD仍为3，因为depth 3v4已低于0.72。\n      有趣的现象：在depth 4+，var_surprisal不再是最区分性特征，因为surprisal的variance\n      已经被\"压缩到底\"——所有深层生成文本的surprisal分布都变得窄且相似。\n      此时zipf_alpha变得相对更区分，因为词频分布的Zipf参数对极深层退化仍有微弱敏感度。\n      这种feature rank变化是Atlas中一个有价值的发现点。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: Extended depth AUC (Pythia, nucleus)\"\n        rows:\n          - pair: \"0v1\"\n            auc: 0.998\n          - pair: \"1v2\"\n            auc: 0.861\n          - pair: \"2v3\"\n            auc: 0.801\n          - pair: \"3v4\"\n            auc: 0.708\n          - pair: \"4v5\"\n            auc: 0.621\n          - pair: \"5v6\"\n            auc: 0.573\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: AUC decay curve across 6 adjacent pairs，EDD=3阈值线标注\"\n      - \"Fig: Top-5 feature importance随depth pair变化的stream plot，显示rank crossover\"\n    analysis: >\n      延伸实验定量确认了depth 3是\"有效区分边界\"——depth 3之后的AUC衰减斜率平缓化，\n      趋向0.5。这为EDD=3提供了额外的经验支持。Feature rank变化的发现值得在Atlas section\n      详细讨论，因为它说明\"退化不只是'所有特征同步衰减'而是'不同退化阶段的主导信号切换'\"。\n\n  - name: \"Granularity ablation\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_012\"\n    description: \"对比binary / 3-class / 4-class / 6-class分类粒度\"\n    expected_results:\n      binary_acc: 0.946\n      binary_auc: 0.983\n      three_class_acc: 0.867\n      three_class_mae: 0.141\n      four_class_acc: 0.823\n      four_class_mae: 0.192\n      six_class_acc: 0.571\n      six_class_mae: 0.462\n      chance_levels: {binary: 0.500, three_class: 0.333, four_class: 0.250, six_class: 0.167}\n      lift_over_chance: {binary: \"+44.6pp\", three_class: \"+53.4pp\", four_class: \"+57.3pp\", six_class: \"+40.4pp\"}\n    result_rationale: >\n      Binary（depth 0 vs depth 1+）几乎perfect（0.946），因为depth 0→1的gap远大于其他对。\n      随粒度增加，absolute acc下降但lift over chance先增后减：4-class的lift最高（+57.3pp），\n      说明4-class是\"信息量/可行性\"的最优平衡点。6-class的lift降至+40.4pp，\n      因为depth 4和depth 5的加入拖累了整体——它们与depth 3高度混淆。\n      3-class（0,1,2+）的0.867说明\"有多深\"这个问题在粗粒度上非常可行。\n      这些数字共同支持论文叙事：ordinal depth estimation在EDD内可行，\n      推荐4-class作为实际应用的粒度选择，6-class数字仅作为upper bound report。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: Granularity ablation (DCOL, pooled)\"\n        rows:\n          - granularity: \"Binary (0 vs 1+)\"\n            acc: 0.946\n            chance: 0.500\n            lift_pp: 44.6\n          - granularity: \"3-class (0,1,2+)\"\n            acc: 0.867\n            chance: 0.333\n            lift_pp: 53.4\n          - granularity: \"4-class (0,1,2,3+)\"\n            acc: 0.823\n            chance: 0.250\n            lift_pp: 57.3\n          - granularity: \"6-class (0-5)\"\n            acc: 0.571\n            chance: 0.167\n            lift_pp: 40.4\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: Accuracy vs granularity折线图，附chance baseline和lift标注\"\n    analysis: >\n      4-class是sweet spot的结论直接支持EDD=3叙事，也回应了reviewer concern \"EDD might be low\"。\n      论文可以argue：4-class粒度（0=原始, 1=first gen, 2=second gen, 3+=deep recursive）\n      在curation场景中已经足够——用户最需要区分的是\"原始vs浅层生成vs深层递归\"。\n\n  - name: \"Downstream curation proof-of-concept\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_013\"\n    description: \"Depth-graduated weighting vs binary filtering，在1B模型fine-tuning上测试\"\n    expected_results:\n      binary_filter_ppl: 18.72\n      graduated_weighting_ppl: 18.14\n      no_filter_ppl: 19.85\n      oracle_depth_weighting_ppl: 17.91\n      ppl_reduction_graduated_vs_binary_pct: 3.1\n      ppl_reduction_graduated_vs_nofilter_pct: 8.6\n      graduated_vs_binary_p_value: 0.038\n      downstream_task_acc_binary: 0.724\n      downstream_task_acc_graduated: 0.731\n      downstream_task_acc_nofilter: 0.703\n    result_rationale: >\n      Graduated weighting（1/k权重，k=predicted depth+1）的PPL比binary低3.1%，\n      处于median的[2,5]范围内。p-value=0.038勉强显著（<0.05），但远未达到强显著。\n      这是因为graduated weighting的优势主要来自对depth 1-2的差异化处理——\n      binary filter将所有\"synthetic\"同等对待，而graduated保留了quality尚可的depth 1内容\n      并只强力down-weight depth 2+。Oracle depth weighting（用真实depth而非predicted）\n      的PPL=17.91比graduated的18.14低，gap=1.3%说明prediction error（DCOL的misclassification）\n      确实影响了curation效果，但graduated仍然明显优于binary。\n      Downstream task acc的差距更小（0.731 vs 0.724），因为PPL的差异在传导到task performance\n      时会被衰减。在median档下，这个proof-of-concept足以\"展示方向\"但不能做强声明。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: Curation comparison\"\n        rows:\n          - method: \"No filter\"\n            ppl: 19.85\n            task_acc: 0.703\n          - method: \"Binary filter (remove synthetic)\"\n            ppl: 18.72\n            task_acc: 0.724\n          - method: \"Graduated weighting (predicted depth)\"\n            ppl: 18.14\n            task_acc: 0.731\n          - method: \"Oracle weighting (true depth)\"\n            ppl: 17.91\n            task_acc: 0.738\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: 4种curation策略的PPL对比bar chart，with error bars\"\n      - \"Fig: Weighting function sensitivity分析——1/k vs 1/k² vs exponential decay\"\n    analysis: >\n      3.1%的PPL reduction和p=0.038的显著性在median档下是\"正向但不强\"的结果。\n      论文应将此section控制在~1页，framing为proof-of-concept，明确stated limitation：\n      (1) 只在一个model scale上测试，(2) graduated vs binary的差距在error bar内有overlap，\n      (3) curation效果依赖depth prediction质量。\n\n  - name: \"7B cross-scale probe\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_014\"\n    description: \"Qwen2.5-7B或Llama-3.1-8B生成3层递归链，用小模型训练的DCOL做zero-shot迁移\"\n    expected_results:\n      zero_shot_transfer_4class_acc: 0.614\n      zero_shot_transfer_6class_acc: 0.372\n      fine_tuned_on_7b_4class_acc: 0.791\n      edd_7b_nucleus: 3\n      edd_7b_temperature: 2\n      auc_0v1_7b: 0.989\n      auc_1v2_7b: 0.824\n      auc_2v3_7b: 0.741\n    result_rationale: >\n      7B模型的生成质量显著高于1-1.5B模型，导致递归退化信号更弱——更好的模型在浅层\n      生成\"更像人类\"的文本，depth信号被压缩。Zero-shot transfer的4-class acc 0.614\n      远低于in-distribution的0.823，说明1.5B模型上学到的表示不能直接迁移到7B。\n      这是因为7B模型的\"depth 1\"文本质量接近1.5B模型的\"depth 0\"，导致decision boundary错位。\n      但fine-tune后恢复到0.791，说明depth信号在7B上仍然存在，只是需要recalibration。\n      EDD在7B上仍为3（nucleus）但temperature降至2，因为7B+temperature的生成多样性\n      使得depth 2→3就已不可区分。这进一步支持了Atlas中\"模型能力越强，EDD越可能降低\"的假设。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: Cross-scale transfer (7B)\"\n        rows:\n          - setting: \"Zero-shot (train on 1-1.5B, test on 7B)\"\n            acc_4class: 0.614\n            acc_6class: 0.372\n          - setting: \"Fine-tuned on 7B data\"\n            acc_4class: 0.791\n            acc_6class: 0.518\n          - setting: \"1-1.5B in-distribution (reference)\"\n            acc_4class: 0.823\n            acc_6class: 0.571\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: 小模型vs大模型的feature分布对比violin plot——7B的分布更紧凑\"\n    analysis: >\n      Cross-scale transfer是limitation而非failure。Zero-shot的gap说明需要scale-aware\n      calibration，但fine-tune后的接近恢复说明depth信号是universal的，只是magnitude不同。\n      论文中这可以framing为future work方向：scale-invariant depth estimation。\n\n  - name: \"Wild-data calibration\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_015\"\n    description: \"DCOL depth scores on RedPajama/Dolma vs perplexity/AlignScore质量代理\"\n    expected_results:\n      spearman_dcol_vs_ppl: 0.341\n      spearman_dcol_vs_alignscore: 0.283\n      spearman_dcol_vs_ppl_p_value: 0.002\n      spearman_dcol_vs_alignscore_p_value: 0.014\n      pct_wild_data_scored_depth0: 0.72\n      pct_wild_data_scored_depth1plus: 0.28\n      pct_wild_data_scored_depth3plus: 0.06\n    result_rationale: >\n      Wild data上没有ground-truth depth，只能用proxy验证。Spearman相关0.341（DCOL score vs PPL）\n      是中等正相关——高DCOL depth score（预测为深层递归）的文本确实倾向于有更高perplexity，\n      但相关性不强，因为wild data中高PPL的原因很多（不只是递归深度还有domain、quality等）。\n      AlignScore的相关更弱（0.283），因为AlignScore衡量的是factual consistency而非statistical\n      degradation——递归深度高不一定意味着factually inconsistent。\n      72%的wild data被scored为depth 0是合理的——大部分web text仍然是人类写的。\n      6%被scored为depth 3+可能overestimate，因为模型在controlled setting训练，\n      wild data中的低质量人类文本可能被误判为深层递归。\n      p-values显著但相关系数中等，符合median档\"有正向信号但不强\"的预期。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: Wild-data correlation with quality proxies\"\n        rows:\n          - proxy: \"Perplexity (GPT-2)\"\n            spearman: 0.341\n            p_value: 0.002\n          - proxy: \"AlignScore\"\n            spearman: 0.283\n            p_value: 0.014\n      - name: \"Table: Predicted depth distribution on RedPajama sample\"\n        rows:\n          - depth: \"0 (human)\"\n            pct: 72\n          - depth: \"1\"\n            pct: 16\n          - depth: \"2\"\n            pct: 6\n          - depth: \"3+\"\n            pct: 6\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: DCOL predicted depth vs perplexity散点图（RedPajama 10K sample），with regression line\"\n      - \"Fig: Predicted depth分布histogram on wild data\"\n    analysis: >\n      Wild-data结果只能作为calibration而非validation。中等相关说明DCOL的depth score\n      在wild setting下有一定语义一致性，但controlled→wild的gap明显。\n      论文应将此作为\"ecological validity probe\"而非core result，\n      明确声明\"controlled setting是primary，wild transfer是future work\"。\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":10200,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":10200},"output_tokens":27,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"59c1aef7-b7d0-4e34-b364-7145a430c46b","uuid":"5ec46c9f-f093-4be3-a3f1-d3ae9fe776c5"}
{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"api_error_status":null,"duration_ms":285616,"duration_api_ms":287103,"num_turns":1,"result":"```yaml\ntier: median\nnarrative_guidance: >\n  EDD≈3是核心科学发现，论文叙事围绕\"ordinal depth estimation在EDD边界内可行\"展开。\n  DCOL优于baseline但优势中等（+3-7pp），叙事重心从方法突破转向\"序数框架+Atlas\"的组合贡献。\n  Atlas权重上升为论文核心——文档化递归退化的边界和模式对model collapse社区直接有用。\n  Claim 3缩减为proof-of-concept。跨模型泛化诚实报告per-rotation结果，弱rotation作为limitation。\n  有效粒度声明降级：6-class数字报告但承认depth 4+坍缩，实际可行粒度为4-class（depths 0-3）。\n\nimagined_experiments:\n  - name: \"OLMo-1B recursive chain benchmark\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_002\"\n    description: \"OLMo-1B在3种策略下生成5层递归链，提取19维统计特征，RF分类\"\n    expected_results:\n      full_4class_acc: 0.754\n      full_4class_acc_ci: [0.740, 0.768]\n      full_mae: 0.268\n      full_auc_0v1: 0.994\n      full_auc_1v2: 0.838\n      full_auc_2v3: 0.771\n      filtered_4class_acc: 0.789\n      filtered_4class_acc_ci: [0.775, 0.803]\n      filtered_mae: 0.225\n      best_model: \"RandomForest\"\n      top_features: [\"var_surprisal\", \"mean_ppl\", \"p90_ppl\", \"zipf_alpha\", \"mean_surprisal\"]\n      feature_dim: 19\n      samples_per_depth_per_strategy: ~1200\n    result_rationale: >\n      OLMo-1B在Dolma上训练，分布与Pythia的Pile有差异。Dolma以清洗后的web text为主，\n      初始生成（depth 0→1）的分布偏移略小于Pythia，导致depth 0v1的AUC微降（0.994 vs 0.998）。\n      但OLMo的Dolma训练使其对web-text domain更稳定，depth 2v3退化信号略弱（0.771 vs 0.801），\n      因为OLMo的生成在浅层更\"像人类\"，深层退化启动更晚。整体4-class acc低于Pythia约3pp，\n      符合median档\"信号真实但模型间有波动\"的预期。var_surprisal仍是最强特征，\n      但zipf_alpha在OLMo上排名上升——OLMo的tokenizer和训练数据使词频分布对递归深度更敏感。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: OLMo-1B per-strategy 4-class accuracy\"\n        rows:\n          - strategy: \"nucleus_p0.95\"\n            acc_4class: 0.768\n            mae: 0.252\n            auc_0v1: 0.995\n            auc_1v2: 0.849\n            auc_2v3: 0.784\n          - strategy: \"temperature_0.9\"\n            acc_4class: 0.741\n            mae: 0.281\n            auc_0v1: 0.993\n            auc_1v2: 0.827\n            auc_2v3: 0.758\n          - strategy: \"topk_50\"\n            acc_4class: 0.752\n            mae: 0.271\n            auc_0v1: 0.994\n            auc_1v2: 0.839\n            auc_2v3: 0.770\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: OLMo per-strategy adjacent-depth AUC曲线，显示3种策略在depth 2→3处均出现明显下降\"\n    analysis: >\n      OLMo结果确认递归退化信号跨模型存在但强度有差异。temperature策略在OLMo上表现最弱，\n      因为τ=0.9引入的随机性与OLMo自身生成的多样性叠加，模糊了深度信号。\n      这预示cross-model泛化中OLMo作为held-out时可能是较难的rotation。\n\n  - name: \"GPT-2 XL recursive chain benchmark\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_003\"\n    description: \"GPT-2 XL 1.5B在3种策略下生成5层递归链，提取19维统计特征，RF分类\"\n    expected_results:\n      full_4class_acc: 0.798\n      full_4class_acc_ci: [0.785, 0.811]\n      full_mae: 0.218\n      full_auc_0v1: 0.998\n      full_auc_1v2: 0.874\n      full_auc_2v3: 0.812\n      filtered_4class_acc: 0.831\n      filtered_4class_acc_ci: [0.818, 0.844]\n      filtered_mae: 0.183\n      best_model: \"RandomForest\"\n      top_features: [\"var_surprisal\", \"p90_ppl\", \"mean_ppl\", \"mean_surprisal\", \"p75_ppl\"]\n      feature_dim: 19\n      samples_per_depth_per_strategy: ~1200\n    result_rationale: >\n      GPT-2 XL是collapse文献中最被研究的模型，其WebText训练集相对较小且老旧。\n      关键：GPT-2 XL的生成能力弱于Pythia和OLMo，递归生成退化更快更明显，\n      导致相邻深度间的统计差异更大。depth 0v1的AUC（0.998）与Pythia持平，\n      但depth 1v2（0.874 vs 0.861）和depth 2v3（0.812 vs 0.801）均高于Pythia。\n      这意味着GPT-2 XL的EDD可能略高于3（但在6-class下仍然depth 4+坍缩）。\n      4-class acc 0.798略高于Pythia的0.782，因为GPT-2 XL的退化信号更强。\n      top features排名与Pythia几乎一致，说明var_surprisal作为核心信号具有跨模型稳定性。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: GPT-2 XL per-strategy 4-class accuracy\"\n        rows:\n          - strategy: \"nucleus_p0.95\"\n            acc_4class: 0.812\n            mae: 0.204\n            auc_0v1: 0.998\n            auc_1v2: 0.885\n            auc_2v3: 0.823\n          - strategy: \"temperature_0.9\"\n            acc_4class: 0.783\n            mae: 0.234\n            auc_0v1: 0.997\n            auc_1v2: 0.861\n            auc_2v3: 0.798\n          - strategy: \"topk_50\"\n            acc_4class: 0.799\n            mae: 0.217\n            auc_0v1: 0.998\n            auc_1v2: 0.876\n            auc_2v3: 0.815\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: GPT-2 XL与Pythia的adjacent-depth AUC对比，GPT-2 XL在所有对上均略高\"\n    analysis: >\n      GPT-2 XL展现最强的深度信号，符合其作为\"能力较弱模型退化更快\"的预期。\n      这对Atlas叙事有利——不同模型的退化速率不同，但模式（monotonic decrease in AUC）一致。\n      GPT-2 XL的强信号也意味着在cross-model实验中，它作为训练集的一部分会贡献最多信息，\n      作为held-out测试集则最容易通过gate。\n\n  - name: \"DCOL contrastive ordinal training\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_004\"\n    description: \"DeBERTa-v3-large编码器 + 多margin N-pair contrastive loss，6-class depth estimation\"\n    expected_results:\n      dcol_6class_acc_pooled: 0.571\n      dcol_6class_acc_ci: [0.556, 0.586]\n      dcol_mae_6class: 0.462\n      dcol_4class_acc: 0.823\n      dcol_4class_acc_ci: [0.811, 0.835]\n      dcol_mae_4class: 0.192\n      dcol_auc_0v1: 0.999\n      dcol_auc_1v2: 0.912\n      dcol_auc_2v3: 0.856\n      dcol_auc_3v4: 0.714\n      dcol_auc_4v5: 0.628\n      best_lr: 2.0e-5\n      best_margin_schedule: \"learned_non_uniform\"\n      convergence_epoch: 7\n      training_hours_actual: 12.5\n    result_rationale: >\n      DCOL利用DeBERTa编码器从原始文本学习表示，contrastive ordinal loss强制相邻深度的embedding\n      距离反映实际退化幅度。6-class pooled acc 0.571处于median范围[0.52,0.62]中段。\n      关键：DCOL相比RF+features的提升集中在depth 1-3的区分（AUC 1v2从0.86→0.91，2v3从0.80→0.86），\n      因为contrastive learning能捕捉features无法编码的微妙语义退化模式。\n      但depth 3v4的AUC仅0.714——刚好在EDD边界上，depth 4v5的0.628接近随机（chance~0.5）。\n      这证实EDD≈3：DCOL在depth 0-3上显著优于RF，但无法突破depth 3+的信号天花板。\n      4-class acc 0.823高于RF的0.782（pooled across 3 models），验证了contrastive learning\n      在EDD内的有效性。non_uniform learned margins优于fixed margins，\n      因为实际inter-depth距离高度不均匀（depth 0→1远大于depth 2→3）。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: DCOL vs RF feature-based, pooled across 3 models × 3 strategies\"\n        rows:\n          - method: \"DCOL (DeBERTa + contrastive)\"\n            acc_6class: 0.571\n            mae_6class: 0.462\n            acc_4class: 0.823\n            mae_4class: 0.192\n          - method: \"RF + 19 features\"\n            acc_6class: 0.497\n            mae_6class: 0.538\n            acc_4class: 0.778\n            mae_4class: 0.241\n          - method: \"CORAL (DeBERTa + fixed margin)\"\n            acc_6class: 0.538\n            mae_6class: 0.491\n            acc_4class: 0.806\n            mae_4class: 0.211\n          - method: \"CE (DeBERTa + cross-entropy)\"\n            acc_6class: 0.519\n            mae_6class: 0.512\n            acc_4class: 0.793\n            mae_4class: 0.224\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: DCOL训练loss曲线 + per-class accuracy随epoch变化，depth 4-5的accuracy在epoch 4后plateau\"\n      - \"Fig: Learned margin值可视化——margin(0,1) >> margin(2,3) >> margin(3,4)，反映退化的非均匀性\"\n    analysis: >\n      DCOL在EDD边界内（depth 0-3）的优势明确，但对depth 4+无能为力。\n      这支持median叙事：方法有效但有天花板，天花板由信号本身（而非方法）决定。\n      CORAL作为ablation的中间点（0.538 vs DCOL 0.571 vs CE 0.519）说明\n      ordinal inductive bias有帮助，learned margins在此基础上进一步提升。\n      但DCOL vs CORAL仅+3.3pp，说明增益部分来自ordinal structure本身而非contrastive learning独有。\n\n  - name: \"Leave-one-model-out generalization\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_005\"\n    description: \"3个rotation：每次留一个模型族作test，用另外两个训练DCOL\"\n    expected_results:\n      rotation_hold_pythia:\n        train_on: [\"OLMo-1B\", \"GPT-2 XL\"]\n        test_on: \"Pythia-1.4B\"\n        acc_6class: 0.483\n        acc_4class: 0.721\n        mae_6class: 0.547\n      rotation_hold_olmo:\n        train_on: [\"Pythia-1.4B\", \"GPT-2 XL\"]\n        test_on: \"OLMo-1B\"\n        acc_6class: 0.421\n        acc_4class: 0.673\n        mae_6class: 0.601\n      rotation_hold_gpt2xl:\n        train_on: [\"Pythia-1.4B\", \"OLMo-1B\"]\n        test_on: \"GPT-2 XL\"\n        acc_6class: 0.507\n        acc_4class: 0.748\n        mae_6class: 0.521\n      cross_model_loo_6class_acc_mean: 0.470\n      cross_model_loo_6class_acc_std: 0.036\n      cross_model_loo_4class_acc_mean: 0.714\n      gate_pass_count: \"2/3 rotations ≥ 0.45 (6-class), OLMo rotation at 0.421 misses\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      跨模型泛化是median档的核心挑战。mean 6-class acc 0.470处于[0.42,0.52]范围内。\n      Hold-OLMo是最弱rotation（0.421，未通过0.45 gate）：OLMo在Dolma上训练，\n      其生成分布与Pile-trained Pythia和WebText-trained GPT-2 XL差异最大。\n      Pythia和GPT-2 XL都在\"early web text\"类型数据上训练，彼此更相似，\n      所以hold-GPT2XL rotation最强（0.507）——Pythia+OLMo的组合已覆盖足够多样性。\n      Hold-Pythia居中（0.483），因为OLMo+GPT2XL的组合提供了合理的训练分布。\n      4-class acc均显著高于6-class，再次确认depth 4+的信号不跨模型迁移。\n      std=0.036反映\"有波动\"的median特征——不是所有rotation都稳定通过。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: Leave-one-model-out 6-class results\"\n        rows:\n          - rotation: \"Hold Pythia\"\n            acc_6class: 0.483\n            acc_4class: 0.721\n            mae: 0.547\n            gate_45: \"PASS\"\n          - rotation: \"Hold OLMo\"\n            acc_6class: 0.421\n            acc_4class: 0.673\n            mae: 0.601\n            gate_45: \"FAIL\"\n          - rotation: \"Hold GPT-2 XL\"\n            acc_6class: 0.507\n            acc_4class: 0.748\n            mae: 0.521\n            gate_45: \"PASS\"\n          - rotation: \"Mean ± std\"\n            acc_6class: \"0.470 ± 0.036\"\n            acc_4class: \"0.714 ± 0.031\"\n            mae: \"0.556 ± 0.033\"\n            gate_45: \"2/3\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: 3-rotation confusion matrices并排，Hold-OLMo显示depth 2和depth 3高度混淆\"\n      - \"Fig: Per-rotation per-depth accuracy heatmap，depth 0在所有rotation上 > 90%\"\n    analysis: >\n      OLMo rotation的失败需要在论文中诚实报告为limitation。叙事可以是：\n      \"跨模型泛化在架构/数据相似的模型间成立，但对训练分布差异大的模型需要域适应\"。\n      4-class acc 0.714 mean说明\"在EDD内的粗粒度估计\"仍然跨模型可行，\n      这支持降级后的Claim 1声明。补充feature importance drift分析解释OLMo为什么难。\n\n  - name: \"Depth Degradation Atlas\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_006\"\n    description: \"9个model×strategy combo的特征单调性分析、EDD计算、跨模型/策略热力图\"\n    expected_results:\n      edd_per_combo:\n        pythia_nucleus: 3\n        pythia_temperature: 3\n        pythia_topk: 3\n        olmo_nucleus: 3\n        olmo_temperature: 2\n        olmo_topk: 3\n        gpt2xl_nucleus: 4\n        gpt2xl_temperature: 3\n        gpt2xl_topk: 3\n      edd_median: 3\n      edd_mean: 3.0\n      edd_min: 2\n      edd_max: 4\n      monotonicity_score_top5_mean: 0.782\n      monotonicity_score_top5_range: [0.71, 0.85]\n      top5_features_by_monotonicity: [\"var_surprisal\", \"p90_ppl\", \"mean_ppl\", \"zipf_alpha\", \"mean_surprisal\"]\n      feature_monotonicity_var_surprisal: 0.847\n      feature_monotonicity_p90_ppl: 0.823\n      feature_monotonicity_mean_ppl: 0.801\n      feature_monotonicity_zipf_alpha: 0.768\n      feature_monotonicity_mean_surprisal: 0.752\n      non_monotonic_combos: [\"olmo_temperature_depth3→4_mean_ppl\", \"pythia_topk_depth4→5_var_surprisal\"]\n      min_adjacent_auc_within_edd: 0.771\n    result_rationale: >\n      EDD median=3横跨9个combo，但分布有意义的变化。GPT-2 XL nucleus是唯一EDD=4的combo，\n      因为GPT-2 XL退化最快（前述），nucleus采样保留了最多信号。OLMo temperature是唯一EDD=2的combo，\n      因为OLMo的生成多样性本就高，叠加temperature的随机性导致depth 2→3的信号就已饱和。\n      这种跨combo的EDD变化本身就是Atlas的核心科学贡献——EDD不是一个固定常数而是取决于模型能力和解码策略。\n      top5特征的单调性得分mean 0.782处于[0.7,0.85]范围。var_surprisal最高（0.847），\n      因为递归生成使surprisal分布progressively narrowing——这是最稳定的退化信号。\n      两个非单调combo出现在depth 3→4之后，符合\"EDD边界后信号坍缩\"的预期。\n      min_adjacent_auc_within_edd=0.771（出现在OLMo temperature的depth 1v2），处于[0.72,0.80]范围。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: EDD per model × strategy\"\n        rows:\n          - model: \"Pythia-1.4B\"\n            nucleus: 3\n            temperature: 3\n            topk: 3\n          - model: \"OLMo-1B\"\n            nucleus: 3\n            temperature: 2\n            topk: 3\n          - model: \"GPT-2 XL\"\n            nucleus: 4\n            temperature: 3\n            topk: 3\n      - name: \"Table: Top-10 feature monotonicity scores (mean across 9 combos)\"\n        rows:\n          - feature: \"var_surprisal\"\n            mono_score: 0.847\n            rank_stability: \"1/9 combos rank 1\"\n          - feature: \"p90_ppl\"\n            mono_score: 0.823\n            rank_stability: \"6/9 combos rank ≤ 3\"\n          - feature: \"mean_ppl\"\n            mono_score: 0.801\n            rank_stability: \"7/9 combos rank ≤ 4\"\n          - feature: \"zipf_alpha\"\n            mono_score: 0.768\n            rank_stability: \"5/9 combos rank ≤ 5\"\n          - feature: \"mean_surprisal\"\n            mono_score: 0.752\n            rank_stability: \"8/9 combos rank ≤ 6\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: 9-panel heatmap（3 models × 3 strategies），每panel显示19个特征在6个depth上的z-score，EDD边界用虚线标注\"\n      - \"Fig: var_surprisal在9个combo上的depth-wise分布boxplot，显示depth 0-3单调递减，depth 4-5重叠\"\n      - \"Fig: EDD boundary可视化——adjacent-depth AUC随depth递减，0.72阈值线标注EDD截断点\"\n      - \"Fig: 非单调异常案例的feature trajectory（OLMo temperature的mean_ppl在depth 3→4回升）\"\n    analysis: >\n      Atlas是median档下论文的核心贡献。EDD=3的中位数意味着\"ordinal depth estimation在4级粒度上可行\"，\n      这本身就是对model collapse社区的直接贡献——之前没有人系统量化\"从哪个depth开始区分变得不可能\"。\n      EDD跨combo的变化（2-4）提供了丰富的分析空间：为什么OLMo+temperature最早饱和？\n      为什么GPT-2 XL+nucleus能多撑一层？这些问题直接关联模型能力和解码策略的交互效应。\n      非单调现象（2/9 combos在EDD之后）可以解释为\"信号坍缩后的噪声震荡\"而非真实的非单调退化。\n\n  - name: \"Leave-one-strategy-out robustness\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_007\"\n    description: \"3个rotation：每次留一种策略作test，用另外两种训练DCOL\"\n    expected_results:\n      rotation_hold_nucleus:\n        train_on: [\"temperature\", \"topk\"]\n        test_on: \"nucleus\"\n        acc_6class: 0.528\n        acc_4class: 0.786\n      rotation_hold_temperature:\n        train_on: [\"nucleus\", \"topk\"]\n        test_on: \"temperature\"\n        acc_6class: 0.492\n        acc_4class: 0.753\n      rotation_hold_topk:\n        train_on: [\"nucleus\", \"temperature\"]\n        test_on: \"topk\"\n        acc_6class: 0.541\n        acc_4class: 0.798\n      strategy_loo_6class_acc_mean: 0.520\n      strategy_loo_6class_acc_std: 0.021\n    result_rationale: >\n      策略间泛化优于模型间泛化（mean 0.520 vs 0.470），因为不同解码策略影响的是生成文本的\n      表面统计特性（多样性、重复率），而递归退化的核心信号（surprisal variance压缩、\n      perplexity drift）跨策略更稳定。Hold-temperature最弱（0.492）是因为temperature采样\n      产生的分布与nucleus/topk的截断采样在尾部行为上差异最大——temperature不截断分布，\n      而是rescale整个logit空间，导致生成文本的统计profile不同。\n      Hold-topk最强（0.541）是因为topk_50与nucleus_0.95在实际效果上最接近\n      （都是尾部截断，只是截断方式不同），所以nucleus训练集已包含了大部分topk的信号。\n      std=0.021远小于cross-model的0.036，说明策略间差异比模型间差异小。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: Leave-one-strategy-out results\"\n        rows:\n          - rotation: \"Hold nucleus\"\n            acc_6class: 0.528\n            acc_4class: 0.786\n          - rotation: \"Hold temperature\"\n            acc_6class: 0.492\n            acc_4class: 0.753\n          - rotation: \"Hold topk\"\n            acc_6class: 0.541\n            acc_4class: 0.798\n          - rotation: \"Mean ± std\"\n            acc_6class: \"0.520 ± 0.021\"\n            acc_4class: \"0.779 ± 0.019\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: Strategy-out vs Model-out泛化gap对比bar chart\"\n    analysis: >\n      策略泛化比模型泛化容易的结论对论文positioning有利——说明depth信号主要与模型能力相关，\n      而非解码策略的artifact。这强化了Atlas中\"模型能力决定EDD\"的叙事。\n      Hold-temperature的相对弱势可引出discussion：temperature采样作为最\"自由\"的策略，\n      其生成文本的统计分布最不受约束，可能需要专门的domain adaptation。\n\n  - name: \"DeBERTa end-to-end classifier\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_008\"\n    description: \"DeBERTa-v3-large直接text→6-class depth分类，无手工特征\"\n    expected_results:\n      e2e_6class_acc: 0.553\n      e2e_6class_acc_ci: [0.537, 0.569]\n      e2e_mae_6class: 0.478\n      e2e_4class_acc: 0.809\n      e2e_4class_acc_ci: [0.796, 0.822]\n      e2e_mae_4class: 0.206\n      e2e_auc_0v1: 0.998\n      e2e_auc_1v2: 0.897\n      e2e_auc_2v3: 0.838\n      e2e_auc_3v4: 0.698\n      e2e_auc_4v5: 0.614\n      training_hours: 9.2\n      best_lr: 1.0e-5\n    result_rationale: >\n      End-to-end DeBERTa（CE loss）的6-class acc 0.553略低于DCOL的0.571，\n      但高于RF+features的0.497。这是median档的典型结果：end-to-end能学到features\n      无法捕捉的语义退化信号（如coherence loss、topic drift），但没有DCOL的ordinal\n      inductive bias，它在相邻深度的区分上不如DCOL精确——特别是depth 2v3（0.838 vs 0.856）\n      和depth 3v4（0.698 vs 0.714）的AUC差距。End-to-end不如DCOL的原因是CE loss\n      将每个class独立对待，不利用ordinal structure，而递归深度本质上是有序的。\n      但end-to-end优于RF说明原始文本中确实存在features未编码的退化信号。\n      这对论文叙事的含义：DCOL = end-to-end表示能力 + ordinal structure，两者都有贡献。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: End-to-end vs DCOL vs RF\"\n        rows:\n          - method: \"DCOL (contrastive ordinal)\"\n            acc_6class: 0.571\n            mae_6class: 0.462\n            acc_4class: 0.823\n          - method: \"DeBERTa E2E (CE)\"\n            acc_6class: 0.553\n            mae_6class: 0.478\n            acc_4class: 0.809\n          - method: \"RF + 19 features\"\n            acc_6class: 0.497\n            mae_6class: 0.538\n            acc_4class: 0.778\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: 三种方法的per-depth accuracy雷达图，DCOL在depth 2-3上优势最明显\"\n    analysis: >\n      DCOL vs E2E仅+1.8pp（6-class），这在median档下说明contrastive ordinal loss的增益\n      存在但不压倒性。论文需要将此差距诚实报告并通过ablation（plan_010）分解贡献来源。\n\n  - name: \"Baseline battery\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_009\"\n    description: \"7个baseline：DivEye features回归、perplexity回归、CORAL、CE、zero-shot LLM、binary ensemble、LOKI features\"\n    expected_results:\n      baselines:\n        diveye_ordinal_regression:\n          acc_6class: 0.432\n          mae_6class: 0.612\n          acc_4class: 0.698\n        perplexity_regression:\n          acc_6class: 0.389\n          mae_6class: 0.673\n          acc_4class: 0.651\n        coral_deberta:\n          acc_6class: 0.538\n          mae_6class: 0.491\n          acc_4class: 0.806\n        ce_deberta:\n          acc_6class: 0.519\n          mae_6class: 0.512\n          acc_4class: 0.793\n        zeroshot_llm_gpt4o:\n          acc_6class: 0.287\n          mae_6class: 0.892\n          acc_4class: 0.418\n        binary_ensemble_cascade:\n          acc_6class: 0.461\n          mae_6class: 0.574\n          acc_4class: 0.723\n        loki_features_regression:\n          acc_6class: 0.408\n          mae_6class: 0.641\n          acc_4class: 0.672\n      best_baseline: \"coral_deberta\"\n      best_baseline_6class_acc: 0.538\n      dcol_delta_over_best_baseline_pp: 3.3\n      dcol_delta_over_best_nonordinal_pp: 5.2\n    result_rationale: >\n      CORAL是最强baseline（0.538），因为它也利用了ordinal structure，与DCOL共享DeBERTa backbone。\n      DCOL vs CORAL的+3.3pp处于median的[3,7]范围下端，说明DCOL的增量贡献（learnable margins +\n      contrastive loss + strategy conditioning）存在但中等。CE DeBERTa次之（0.519），\n      说明DeBERTa的表示能力本身就很强，ordinal bias带来的额外增益约2pp。\n      DivEye features（0.432）比RF+19 features（0.497）低，因为DivEye的特征是为binary detection\n      设计的，缺少var_surprisal等对depth敏感的特征。Zero-shot LLM表现最差（0.287，接近\n      6-class chance 16.7%但显著高于），说明LLM的深度判断能力很弱——深度不是surface-level可感知的属性。\n      Binary ensemble cascade（先判binary再细分）达到0.461，优于feature regression但弱于\n      end-to-end方法，因为cascade的error propagation导致浅层误差累积。\n      DCOL delta +3.3pp在median范围内偏低，叙事需要强调\"框架+Atlas\"而非\"方法突破\"。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: Full baseline comparison (pooled across 3 models × 3 strategies)\"\n        rows:\n          - method: \"DCOL (ours)\"\n            acc_6class: 0.571\n            mae_6class: 0.462\n            acc_4class: 0.823\n            delta_vs_best: \"+3.3pp\"\n          - method: \"CORAL (DeBERTa)\"\n            acc_6class: 0.538\n            mae_6class: 0.491\n            acc_4class: 0.806\n            delta_vs_best: \"—\"\n          - method: \"CE (DeBERTa)\"\n            acc_6class: 0.519\n            mae_6class: 0.512\n            acc_4class: 0.793\n            delta_vs_best: \"-1.9pp\"\n          - method: \"RF + 19 features\"\n            acc_6class: 0.497\n            mae_6class: 0.538\n            acc_4class: 0.778\n            delta_vs_best: \"-4.1pp\"\n          - method: \"Binary cascade\"\n            acc_6class: 0.461\n            mae_6class: 0.574\n            acc_4class: 0.723\n            delta_vs_best: \"-7.7pp\"\n          - method: \"DivEye features\"\n            acc_6class: 0.432\n            mae_6class: 0.612\n            acc_4class: 0.698\n            delta_vs_best: \"-10.6pp\"\n          - method: \"LOKI features\"\n            acc_6class: 0.408\n            mae_6class: 0.641\n            acc_4class: 0.672\n            delta_vs_best: \"-13.0pp\"\n          - method: \"Perplexity regression\"\n            acc_6class: 0.389\n            mae_6class: 0.673\n            acc_4class: 0.651\n            delta_vs_best: \"-14.9pp\"\n          - method: \"Zero-shot GPT-4o\"\n            acc_6class: 0.287\n            mae_6class: 0.892\n            acc_4class: 0.418\n            delta_vs_best: \"-25.1pp\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: 所有方法的6-class acc bar chart，按性能排序，chance line标注\"\n      - \"Fig: MAE vs accuracy scatter plot，DCOL在Pareto前沿\"\n    analysis: >\n      Baseline battery确认DCOL优于所有baseline但优势中等。CORAL作为最强competitor\n      说明ordinal structure是关键——DCOL的额外+3.3pp来自learned margins和contrastive learning，\n      但大部分gain来自ordinal formulation本身。这强化median叙事的重心：\n      \"ordinal框架是核心贡献，DCOL是该框架下的一个strong实现\"。\n      Zero-shot LLM的失败是一个有趣的negative result，值得在paper中简短讨论。\n\n  - name: \"DCOL component ablation\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_010\"\n    description: \"移除surprisal anchors / learnable margins / strategy conditioning各一个，测量增量贡献\"\n    expected_results:\n      full_dcol: {acc_6class: 0.571, mae_6class: 0.462}\n      ablation_no_surprisal_anchors: {acc_6class: 0.558, mae_6class: 0.475, delta_pp: -1.3}\n      ablation_no_learnable_margins: {acc_6class: 0.547, mae_6class: 0.485, delta_pp: -2.4}\n      ablation_no_strategy_conditioning: {acc_6class: 0.562, mae_6class: 0.469, delta_pp: -0.9}\n      ablation_none_of_three: {acc_6class: 0.531, mae_6class: 0.498, delta_pp: -4.0}\n    result_rationale: >\n      Learnable margins的消融影响最大（-2.4pp），因为inter-depth距离的非均匀性是\n      递归退化的核心特征——fixed margins迫使模型假设所有相邻depth等距，这与实际不符。\n      Surprisal anchors的消融影响次之（-1.3pp），因为var_surprisal是最强特征，\n      将其嵌入anchor selection有助于contrastive learning聚焦于最有信息量的样本对。\n      Strategy conditioning影响最小（-0.9pp），因为在pooled setting下策略间差异\n      已经被训练数据的多样性部分覆盖——conditioning的主要作用是在per-strategy evaluation\n      上提升，pooled数字上反映较弱。三个组件全部移除等价于vanilla DeBERTa + N-pair loss，\n      acc降至0.531，仍高于CORAL（0.538→此处应低于CORAL），说明N-pair contrastive loss\n      本身相比CORAL的rank loss有约-0.7pp的差距，三个text-specific modifications\n      弥补了这个差距并额外提升+4.0pp。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: DCOL ablation\"\n        rows:\n          - variant: \"Full DCOL\"\n            acc_6class: 0.571\n            delta: \"—\"\n          - variant: \"– strategy conditioning\"\n            acc_6class: 0.562\n            delta: \"-0.9\"\n          - variant: \"– surprisal anchors\"\n            acc_6class: 0.558\n            delta: \"-1.3\"\n          - variant: \"– learnable margins\"\n            acc_6class: 0.547\n            delta: \"-2.4\"\n          - variant: \"– all three (vanilla contrastive)\"\n            acc_6class: 0.531\n            delta: \"-4.0\"\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: Ablation waterfall chart，从vanilla到full DCOL的累积增益\"\n    analysis: >\n      每个组件贡献1-2.4pp，没有单一组件是决定性的。这对median叙事的含义：\n      DCOL的三个text-specific modifications各自有小但一致的贡献，\n      组合起来提供了4pp的总增益。论文应将此framing为\"method engineering\"而非\"method breakthrough\"。\n\n  - name: \"Depth extension to 5+ generations and EDD analysis\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_011\"\n    description: \"Pythia链延伸到depth 5，分析depth 3-5的信号饱和\"\n    expected_results:\n      pythia_extended_auc_3v4: 0.708\n      pythia_extended_auc_4v5: 0.621\n      pythia_extended_auc_5v6: 0.573\n      feature_overlap_depth4_5_bhattacharyya: 0.82\n      feature_overlap_depth5_6_bhattacharyya: 0.91\n      edd_pythia_extended: 3\n      depth4_5_top_feature_rank_change: \"zipf_alpha从rank 4升至rank 2，var_surprisal从rank 1降至rank 3\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      延伸到depth 5-6后，AUC持续下降：3v4=0.708（已低于原EDD阈值0.72），4v5=0.621，\n      5v6=0.573（接近random的0.5）。Bhattacharyya overlap从depth 4-5的0.82升至depth 5-6的0.91，\n      说明特征分布高度重叠。EDD仍为3，因为depth 3v4已低于0.72。\n      有趣的现象：在depth 4+，var_surprisal不再是最区分性特征，因为surprisal的variance\n      已经被\"压缩到底\"——所有深层生成文本的surprisal分布都变得窄且相似。\n      此时zipf_alpha变得相对更区分，因为词频分布的Zipf参数对极深层退化仍有微弱敏感度。\n      这种feature rank变化是Atlas中一个有价值的发现点。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: Extended depth AUC (Pythia, nucleus)\"\n        rows:\n          - pair: \"0v1\"\n            auc: 0.998\n          - pair: \"1v2\"\n            auc: 0.861\n          - pair: \"2v3\"\n            auc: 0.801\n          - pair: \"3v4\"\n            auc: 0.708\n          - pair: \"4v5\"\n            auc: 0.621\n          - pair: \"5v6\"\n            auc: 0.573\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: AUC decay curve across 6 adjacent pairs，EDD=3阈值线标注\"\n      - \"Fig: Top-5 feature importance随depth pair变化的stream plot，显示rank crossover\"\n    analysis: >\n      延伸实验定量确认了depth 3是\"有效区分边界\"——depth 3之后的AUC衰减斜率平缓化，\n      趋向0.5。这为EDD=3提供了额外的经验支持。Feature rank变化的发现值得在Atlas section\n      详细讨论，因为它说明\"退化不只是'所有特征同步衰减'而是'不同退化阶段的主导信号切换'\"。\n\n  - name: \"Granularity ablation\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_012\"\n    description: \"对比binary / 3-class / 4-class / 6-class分类粒度\"\n    expected_results:\n      binary_acc: 0.946\n      binary_auc: 0.983\n      three_class_acc: 0.867\n      three_class_mae: 0.141\n      four_class_acc: 0.823\n      four_class_mae: 0.192\n      six_class_acc: 0.571\n      six_class_mae: 0.462\n      chance_levels: {binary: 0.500, three_class: 0.333, four_class: 0.250, six_class: 0.167}\n      lift_over_chance: {binary: \"+44.6pp\", three_class: \"+53.4pp\", four_class: \"+57.3pp\", six_class: \"+40.4pp\"}\n    result_rationale: >\n      Binary（depth 0 vs depth 1+）几乎perfect（0.946），因为depth 0→1的gap远大于其他对。\n      随粒度增加，absolute acc下降但lift over chance先增后减：4-class的lift最高（+57.3pp），\n      说明4-class是\"信息量/可行性\"的最优平衡点。6-class的lift降至+40.4pp，\n      因为depth 4和depth 5的加入拖累了整体——它们与depth 3高度混淆。\n      3-class（0,1,2+）的0.867说明\"有多深\"这个问题在粗粒度上非常可行。\n      这些数字共同支持论文叙事：ordinal depth estimation在EDD内可行，\n      推荐4-class作为实际应用的粒度选择，6-class数字仅作为upper bound report。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: Granularity ablation (DCOL, pooled)\"\n        rows:\n          - granularity: \"Binary (0 vs 1+)\"\n            acc: 0.946\n            chance: 0.500\n            lift_pp: 44.6\n          - granularity: \"3-class (0,1,2+)\"\n            acc: 0.867\n            chance: 0.333\n            lift_pp: 53.4\n          - granularity: \"4-class (0,1,2,3+)\"\n            acc: 0.823\n            chance: 0.250\n            lift_pp: 57.3\n          - granularity: \"6-class (0-5)\"\n            acc: 0.571\n            chance: 0.167\n            lift_pp: 40.4\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: Accuracy vs granularity折线图，附chance baseline和lift标注\"\n    analysis: >\n      4-class是sweet spot的结论直接支持EDD=3叙事，也回应了reviewer concern \"EDD might be low\"。\n      论文可以argue：4-class粒度（0=原始, 1=first gen, 2=second gen, 3+=deep recursive）\n      在curation场景中已经足够——用户最需要区分的是\"原始vs浅层生成vs深层递归\"。\n\n  - name: \"Downstream curation proof-of-concept\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_013\"\n    description: \"Depth-graduated weighting vs binary filtering，在1B模型fine-tuning上测试\"\n    expected_results:\n      binary_filter_ppl: 18.72\n      graduated_weighting_ppl: 18.14\n      no_filter_ppl: 19.85\n      oracle_depth_weighting_ppl: 17.91\n      ppl_reduction_graduated_vs_binary_pct: 3.1\n      ppl_reduction_graduated_vs_nofilter_pct: 8.6\n      graduated_vs_binary_p_value: 0.038\n      downstream_task_acc_binary: 0.724\n      downstream_task_acc_graduated: 0.731\n      downstream_task_acc_nofilter: 0.703\n    result_rationale: >\n      Graduated weighting（1/k权重，k=predicted depth+1）的PPL比binary低3.1%，\n      处于median的[2,5]范围内。p-value=0.038勉强显著（<0.05），但远未达到强显著。\n      这是因为graduated weighting的优势主要来自对depth 1-2的差异化处理——\n      binary filter将所有\"synthetic\"同等对待，而graduated保留了quality尚可的depth 1内容\n      并只强力down-weight depth 2+。Oracle depth weighting（用真实depth而非predicted）\n      的PPL=17.91比graduated的18.14低，gap=1.3%说明prediction error（DCOL的misclassification）\n      确实影响了curation效果，但graduated仍然明显优于binary。\n      Downstream task acc的差距更小（0.731 vs 0.724），因为PPL的差异在传导到task performance\n      时会被衰减。在median档下，这个proof-of-concept足以\"展示方向\"但不能做强声明。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: Curation comparison\"\n        rows:\n          - method: \"No filter\"\n            ppl: 19.85\n            task_acc: 0.703\n          - method: \"Binary filter (remove synthetic)\"\n            ppl: 18.72\n            task_acc: 0.724\n          - method: \"Graduated weighting (predicted depth)\"\n            ppl: 18.14\n            task_acc: 0.731\n          - method: \"Oracle weighting (true depth)\"\n            ppl: 17.91\n            task_acc: 0.738\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: 4种curation策略的PPL对比bar chart，with error bars\"\n      - \"Fig: Weighting function sensitivity分析——1/k vs 1/k² vs exponential decay\"\n    analysis: >\n      3.1%的PPL reduction和p=0.038的显著性在median档下是\"正向但不强\"的结果。\n      论文应将此section控制在~1页，framing为proof-of-concept，明确stated limitation：\n      (1) 只在一个model scale上测试，(2) graduated vs binary的差距在error bar内有overlap，\n      (3) curation效果依赖depth prediction质量。\n\n  - name: \"7B cross-scale probe\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_014\"\n    description: \"Qwen2.5-7B或Llama-3.1-8B生成3层递归链，用小模型训练的DCOL做zero-shot迁移\"\n    expected_results:\n      zero_shot_transfer_4class_acc: 0.614\n      zero_shot_transfer_6class_acc: 0.372\n      fine_tuned_on_7b_4class_acc: 0.791\n      edd_7b_nucleus: 3\n      edd_7b_temperature: 2\n      auc_0v1_7b: 0.989\n      auc_1v2_7b: 0.824\n      auc_2v3_7b: 0.741\n    result_rationale: >\n      7B模型的生成质量显著高于1-1.5B模型，导致递归退化信号更弱——更好的模型在浅层\n      生成\"更像人类\"的文本，depth信号被压缩。Zero-shot transfer的4-class acc 0.614\n      远低于in-distribution的0.823，说明1.5B模型上学到的表示不能直接迁移到7B。\n      这是因为7B模型的\"depth 1\"文本质量接近1.5B模型的\"depth 0\"，导致decision boundary错位。\n      但fine-tune后恢复到0.791，说明depth信号在7B上仍然存在，只是需要recalibration。\n      EDD在7B上仍为3（nucleus）但temperature降至2，因为7B+temperature的生成多样性\n      使得depth 2→3就已不可区分。这进一步支持了Atlas中\"模型能力越强，EDD越可能降低\"的假设。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: Cross-scale transfer (7B)\"\n        rows:\n          - setting: \"Zero-shot (train on 1-1.5B, test on 7B)\"\n            acc_4class: 0.614\n            acc_6class: 0.372\n          - setting: \"Fine-tuned on 7B data\"\n            acc_4class: 0.791\n            acc_6class: 0.518\n          - setting: \"1-1.5B in-distribution (reference)\"\n            acc_4class: 0.823\n            acc_6class: 0.571\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: 小模型vs大模型的feature分布对比violin plot——7B的分布更紧凑\"\n    analysis: >\n      Cross-scale transfer是limitation而非failure。Zero-shot的gap说明需要scale-aware\n      calibration，但fine-tune后的接近恢复说明depth信号是universal的，只是magnitude不同。\n      论文中这可以framing为future work方向：scale-invariant depth estimation。\n\n  - name: \"Wild-data calibration\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_015\"\n    description: \"DCOL depth scores on RedPajama/Dolma vs perplexity/AlignScore质量代理\"\n    expected_results:\n      spearman_dcol_vs_ppl: 0.341\n      spearman_dcol_vs_alignscore: 0.283\n      spearman_dcol_vs_ppl_p_value: 0.002\n      spearman_dcol_vs_alignscore_p_value: 0.014\n      pct_wild_data_scored_depth0: 0.72\n      pct_wild_data_scored_depth1plus: 0.28\n      pct_wild_data_scored_depth3plus: 0.06\n    result_rationale: >\n      Wild data上没有ground-truth depth，只能用proxy验证。Spearman相关0.341（DCOL score vs PPL）\n      是中等正相关——高DCOL depth score（预测为深层递归）的文本确实倾向于有更高perplexity，\n      但相关性不强，因为wild data中高PPL的原因很多（不只是递归深度还有domain、quality等）。\n      AlignScore的相关更弱（0.283），因为AlignScore衡量的是factual consistency而非statistical\n      degradation——递归深度高不一定意味着factually inconsistent。\n      72%的wild data被scored为depth 0是合理的——大部分web text仍然是人类写的。\n      6%被scored为depth 3+可能overestimate，因为模型在controlled setting训练，\n      wild data中的低质量人类文本可能被误判为深层递归。\n      p-values显著但相关系数中等，符合median档\"有正向信号但不强\"的预期。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: Wild-data correlation with quality proxies\"\n        rows:\n          - proxy: \"Perplexity (GPT-2)\"\n            spearman: 0.341\n            p_value: 0.002\n          - proxy: \"AlignScore\"\n            spearman: 0.283\n            p_value: 0.014\n      - name: \"Table: Predicted depth distribution on RedPajama sample\"\n        rows:\n          - depth: \"0 (human)\"\n            pct: 72\n          - depth: \"1\"\n            pct: 16\n          - depth: \"2\"\n            pct: 6\n          - depth: \"3+\"\n            pct: 6\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: DCOL predicted depth vs perplexity散点图（RedPajama 10K sample），with regression line\"\n      - \"Fig: Predicted depth分布histogram on wild data\"\n    analysis: >\n      Wild-data结果只能作为calibration而非validation。中等相关说明DCOL的depth score\n      在wild setting下有一定语义一致性，但controlled→wild的gap明显。\n      论文应将此作为\"ecological validity probe\"而非core result，\n      明确声明\"controlled setting是primary，wild transfer是future work\"。\n```","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"59c1aef7-b7d0-4e34-b364-7145a430c46b","total_cost_usd":0.4653935,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":10200,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"output_tokens":15618,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":10200,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":15618,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation_input_tokens":10200,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":10200},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":5163,"outputTokens":20,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.005263,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000},"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":15618,"cacheReadInputTokens":11841,"cacheCreationInputTokens":10200,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.4601305,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"8453b4bb-b5ec-4fbb-b1dc-2a21523dbbb1"}
